# keyring-key-rename: token keyed by user slug (not hostname) is found.
#
# Pre-bug (08b3d9a): the keyring entry was stored under the hostname key
# ("bitbottle:git.example.com"), so every read by user slug would miss it.
# Post-fix: key is ("bitbottle", user_slug).
#
# This test verifies the current canonical shape: hosts.yml has no inline
# token (post-migrate shape), but the keyring holds the token under the
# user slug. auth status must succeed by falling back to the keyring.

bb-fake server

# Simulate the post-migrate shape: remove the inline token from hosts.yml
# by running auth migrate, which moves the token to the keyring under the
# user slug key.
bitbottle auth migrate -k
stdout 'token migrated to keyring'

# Now hosts.yml has no inline token. auth status must still succeed by
# finding the token in the keyring under key ("bitbottle", "testuser").
bitbottle auth status -k
stdout 'Logged in as testuser'
stdout 'Token in keyring: yes'

# No warning now — the token is no longer in hosts.yml.
! stderr 'warning: token found in hosts.yml'
